===''Pokémon the Series''===
====''[[M01|Mewtwo Strikes Back]]''====
In ''[[M01|Mewtwo Strikes Back]]'', a group of Scientists assisted {{an|Dr. Fuji}} in the creation of {{OBP|Mewtwo|M01}}. Mewtwo eventually broke free and destroyed the lab, leaving their status unknown.

===={{aniseries|DP}}====
In ''[[DP050|Tag! We're It...!]]'', a Scientist competed in the [[Hearthome City Tag Battle Competition]]. He was partnered with an {{tc|Ace Trainer}} and was one of {{Ash}}'s and [[Paul]]'s opponents. He ended up getting defeated.

In a flashback in ''[[DP071|Pokémon Ranger and the Kidnapped Riolu! (Part 1)]]'', a Scientist watched as the [[Aura Sphere Riolu]] was taken away from {{OBP|J's client|DP071}}'s henchmen.

In ''[[DP124|To Thine Own Pokémon Be True!]]'', a Scientist competed in the [[Pokémon Ping Pong Tournament]] with his {{p|Alakazam}}. He was {{an|Dawn}} and {{TP|Dawn|Ambipom}}'s first opponent and wound up getting defeated.

===={{aniseries|XY}}====
In ''[[XY023|Coming Back into the Cold!]]'', the appearance of [[Thaddeus]], a researcher at the {{DL|Ambrette Town|Fossil Lab|Ambrette Fossil Lab}}, was based on that of Scientists in {{g|X and Y}}.

A group of Scientists appeared in ''[[XY087|The Tiny Caretaker!]]''.

====''[[M21|The Power of Us]]''====
A group of Scientists appeared in the {{pkmn|movie}} ''[[M21|The Power of Us]]''.

A group of Scientists appeared in the movie ''[[M22|Mewtwo Strikes Back—Evolution]]'', which is a remake of ''[[M01|Mewtwo Strikes Back]]''.

===={{aniseries|JN}}====
In ''[[JN047|Crowning the Chow Crusher!]]'', a Scientist participated in the [[Pokémon Grand Eating Contest]]. He managed to get to the second round but ended up losing to [[Goh]] and his {{TP|Goh|Skwovet}}.

